<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Desc reinstated.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Desc reinstated.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Merrill Lynch said on Monday it had reinstated coverage of Mexico's Desc Sociedad de Fomento Industrial SA de CV with a rating of near-term accumulate and long-term buy.</p>
<p>-- &quot;The company appears well-positioned for a recovery in the domestic economy, as well as from consolidation in the international auto parts business, as production is shifted to low-cost countries like Mexico,&quot; Merrill Lynch said in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Trading at 7.1x and 5.9x prospective EV/EBITDA for 1997 and 1998, the shares are attractive, in our opinion.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's American Depositary Receipts closed at 26 on Monday in New York.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
